Q3 - grep -w alone is not enough when dots are regex wildcards

$ grep -w 203.0.113.10 fake.log
203x0y113z10
203.0.113.10
Exit code: 0

$ grep -wF 203.0.113.10 fake.log
203.0.113.10
Exit code: 0
grep -w still matches 203x0y113z10, because unescaped dots match any character. -F makes the dots literal.
